@page "/privacy"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Privacy</PageTitle>

<section class="page-heading">
    <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</span>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h3" HtmlTag="h1">Inquiry data and your choices</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">How Creative Listing Studio handles information submitted on a public property page.</MudText>
    </div>
</section>

<MudPaper Class="pa-6">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2">Information collected</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
        A property inquiry records the name, email address, optional phone number, message, contact preference,
        referring campaign source, and the separate email or SMS consent choices submitted with the form.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2">How it is used</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
        The real-estate organization that published the property uses the information to answer the inquiry and manage
        follow-up. Marketing consent is optional and is not required to ask about a property. Creative Listing Studio does not
        sell public-inquiry data or use it to infer protected personal characteristics.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2">Retention and requests</MudText>
    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
        The publishing organization controls its lead records and can permanently delete an inquiry and its activity
        history. To request access, correction, or deletion, contact the agent or organization that shared the listing.
        You can also withdraw marketing consent through any follow-up communication you receive.
    </MudText>

    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mud-text-secondary">Lead-consent notice version @ILeadGenerationService.ConsentVersion.</MudText>
</MudPaper>
